{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The outcomes of the two lotteries are: Lottery A has outcomes of 1000 and 0, while Lottery B has a single outcome of 500. The pairwise differences between outcomes are computed by comparing each outcome of Lottery A with each outcome of Lottery B. There are two such pairs: (1000, 500) and (0, 500). The differences are (1000 - 500) = +500 and (0 - 500) = -500. The sum of these differences is +500 - 500 = 0. Since the sum is zero, the decision reason would be indifferent between the two lotteries. Thus, the reason evaluates the sum of pairwise outcome differences and, in this case, yields indifference.",
